# The fewest functions bin/rig-oracle must decide in each set of
# test/run's oracle tests; raise a floor when the oracle grows.
# The oracle decides header subjects that are made values, parts of
# made values, and branching values, `unique` types, Cells and Signals,
# `defer` and `errdefer` bodies, inlined at each exit of their scope,
# handles (`*T`, `~T`), closures, stack and owned, whose bodies it
# checks as functions of their own, generic bodies, and calls of generic
# code at owners where those bodies never copy a type parameter, held
# header parts, payload views, containers of views and write
# views, every element a place, re-pointed write views, and clones, so
# each floor is what it decides now. A value holding a Cell lives only
# behind `*`, and a write view is never stored inside a value, so the
# programs that hold either by value stop in sema, before either
# checker decides them. A header whose subject makes a temporary and
# reaches no place is rejected in sema (`rejectHeaderCopy`), so the
# corpus programs that have one stop there too.
